faq:
  title: Frequently Asked Questions
  list:
    - question: Can I try it now?
      answer: >-
        Yes. The extension is open for testing at <a href="{app}">app.einvoices.ae</a>. Open the
        Extensions screen in an up-to-date copy of Manager, choose eInvoices.ae and create an account.
        You can then send your own sales invoices and credit notes as test e-invoices in the sandbox.
        They go from a test sender to a test receiver, so nothing reaches your customers or the
        Federal Tax Authority. Testing is free.
    - question: When can I send real e-invoices?
      answer: >-
        In December 2026, before the first mandatory date of 1 January 2027. Until then the extension
        works in the sandbox only, and the trial covers sending; receiving comes with the live
        release.
    - question: What is the UAE eInvoicing mandate?
      answer: >-
        Businesses in the UAE have to exchange invoices as structured electronic documents instead of
        PDFs or paper. Each invoice is sent through an Accredited Service Provider over the Peppol
        network in the PINT AE format, and its tax data is reported to the Federal Tax Authority.
    - question: When do I have to start?
      answer: >-
        It depends on your revenue. Businesses with revenue of AED 50 million or more start on
        1 January 2027, and other businesses on 1 July 2027. See the <a href="#deadlines">deadlines</a>
        above.
    - question: What counts as a legal entity?
      answer: >-
        Each company that issues invoices under its own name and Tax Registration Number. If you keep
        the books of three companies in Manager, that is three legal entities, at AED {price} per month
        each.
    - question: Do I need to change how I use Manager?
      answer: >-
        No. You keep creating invoices in Manager as you do now. The extension turns them into
        e-invoices and sends them.
  help: How do I get help?
  helpAnswer: Email
